card.statement:
It is easy to see that for all $i$, $1\le i \le n$:

\begin{equation}
\begin{array}{l}
\qquad z_{i}=1+\sum_{j=1}^{i} (q_{j}-1)y_{j} x_{j}
\qquad\mbox{and}\qquad z_{i}=z_{i-1}+(q_{i}-1)y_{i}x_{i}.
\end{array}
\end{equation}

As a consequence, relations (<<ref:awqm-2>>) read:

\begin{equation}
\begin{array}{l}
\forall i, 1\le i \le n, \;\; x_{i} y_{i} -q_{i} y_{i} x_{i} =z_{i-1}
\end{array}
\end{equation}
